SWEET CHG P3 (patch 0287, charger phase 3): boot-arg sweetchgicl=900 (default OFF, needs sweetchgi2c=1) raises the charger input limit CNFG_09 CHGIN_ILIM from 500 mA to 875 mA (code 0x22), because chg-p2 showed charging at the 500 mA SDP limit is below the iOS load (net discharge); sweetchgicl=500 puts it back (0x13). THE ONLY CHIP WRITES OF THE SERIES (HW-WRITE, for the Opus reviewer; review docs/reviews/chg-0287-review.md F1-F8 fixed here). One I2C write of two bytes to the charger 0x69: [0xC2, (old & 0x80) | 0x22] (setter 0x04 + (875000-125000)/25000, getter 100 + (0x22-3) x 25; note 3 CNFG_09; BMS max77759_charger.c:1445-1499). No CNFG_06 unlock (driver writes CNFG_09 without it, BMS :319-368; CNFG_06 is 0x0C = unlocked on this phone, logged in the preflight row). Read back; a mismatch restores the old value once, logs a GAP and stops all transfers. F1: with this boot-arg only, sweet_usb.c sends bMaxPower 112 (896 mA) in the SuperSpeed configuration descriptor instead of 62 (Android declares 896 mA before it draws 900: GS composite.c:493-511, 952-967; usb_psy.c:31-38, 254-259); sweet_usb_ss_configured() requires the byte actually sent and a SuperSpeed configuration; the flag is cleared at disconnect, bus reset and gadget restart. F2: the samples and a watcher for the rest of the boot restore the old CNFG_09 (once) when the SuperSpeed link or TCPC CHGTYP is lost. Preconditions (GAP and no write otherwise): phase 2 finished with 0 errors and identity checks passed; phase-1 gate + controller idle; the accessor; TCPC CHGTYP SDP/CDP; CNFG_00 MODE 4 or 5; CNFG_09 NO_AUTOIBUS = 1 and ILIM code 4..0x21. Then FG Current/VCell every 30 s for 5 minutes (`SWEET CHG P3: t=..`). i2c_msg gains the write-with-STOP form (len 2) used only by i2c_cnfg09_write. Phase 2 logs a GAP when ILIM is above 500 mA at boot. Never written: CNFG_00/02/04/06/12/18, any bit-3 mode, any other chip. Applies after 0284. Host test: tools/test_chg_icl.py.

